---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import harbour from "../assets/khoist-harbour.png";
---

<div class="khoist-intro">
  <div>
    <p>
      KHoist describes data products as Kubernetes resources. It records who owns a
      product, the APIs it exposes and the products it depends on. A controller
      reports readiness; a read-only registry makes those descriptions available
      to people and applications.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your services keep their data, credentials and query APIs. Your applications
      own their user interfaces and access decisions.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Image
    src={harbour}
    alt="An orange harbour crane hoists connected data-product blocks above the water."
    width={576}
    widths={[360, 576, 768]}
    sizes="(min-width: 70rem) 22rem, (min-width: 50rem) 18rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
    loading="eager"
    format="webp"
  />
</div>
